-- title:
--   Symmetry of the pair height pairHt
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $r$ be a natural number, let $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to F$ be a family of $r$ elements of $F$, and let $v, w$ be two places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in the sense of the project's `Place` structure: valuation subrings of $F$ containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ under the structure map, distinct from $F$ itself, and principal ideal rings. The assertion is the identity $\mathrm{pairHt}\,s\,v\,w = \mathrm{pairHt}\,s\,w\,v$, where by definition $\mathrm{pairHt}\,s\,v\,w$ is $\mathrm{pointHt}\,s\,v + \mathrm{pointHt}\,s\,w - \mathrm{absLogHeight}(\mathrm{chordVec}\,s\,v\,w)$, with $\mathrm{pointHt}\,s\,v = \mathrm{absLogHeight}(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v)$ the absolute logarithmic height of the coordinate vector $\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{Fin}\,r}$ attached to $s$ and $v$, and $\mathrm{chordVec}\,s\,v\,w$ the family of $2\times 2$ minors indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,r \times \mathrm{Fin}\,r$, whose value at $(i,j)$ is $(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v)_i(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,w)_j - (\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v)_j(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,w)_i$. Here $\mathrm{absLogHeight}$ of a finite family $x$ of algebraic numbers is $[\mathbb{Q}(x):\mathbb{Q}]^{-1}$ times the logarithmic height of $x$ computed inside the field $\mathbb{Q}(x)$ generated by its entries. No hypothesis beyond the above is imposed on $s$, $v$ or $w$.
--
--   The symmetry of the pair height, the two-variable quantity built from the point heights of two places and the height of the vector of $2\times 2$ minors of their coordinate vectors; interchanging the two places negates each minor, which leaves the absolute logarithmic height unchanged. It is used in the height-form estimates on $J_0(N)$, where the cross terms of the quadratic height form are rewritten with the pairing taken in a single order, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_pairHt_comm.lean

